From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:25:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The Pokémon League's south ridge gets its east wall (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Pokémon League's south map's east ridge stops 4 tiles above the
ground east of it with nothing between, a black slit seen from Route
224 (the DS's view never reached it). The north map's east wall there is
drawn again south of it, 13 tiles lower (sPortMapPieces), from z 576 to
604; from inside the League nothing changes.
---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 3945d486..16be9569 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -6744,6 +6744,8 @@ static const PortMapPiece sPortMapPieces[] = {
     { 0, 676, 4, { 174, 204, 62, 68 }, 6, 0, 1, 1, 0, 32, 0, -64, 1, 0 },    // (Route 209: its river's top, x 538-541: the north-west corner and the top)
     { 0, 677, 3, { 76, 82, 62, 68 }, 4, 0, 1, 1, 0, -96, 0, -64, 1, 0 },     // (the north-east corner, from the map east of it)
     { 0, 526, 0, { 0, 256, 64, 128 }, 4, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, -128, 1, 0 },  // (Route 210 North's south-west map: the low filler's ground under its last rows, seen under its terraces' ends)
+    { 0, 536, 1, { 228, 236, 144, 208 }, 7, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, -104, 112, 3, 64 }, // (the Pokemon League's south map: its east ridge, x 860, stops 4 tiles above the ground east of it, nothing between (seen from Route 224): the north map's east wall there, 13 tiles lower, z 576-599)
+    { 0, 536, 1, { 228, 236, 144, 208 }, 7, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, -104, 280, 1, 0 },  // (and z 597-604)
     { 0, 669, 2, { 32, 64, 0, 8 }, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, -288, 0, 224, 8, 0, 32 },   // (Route 207's west map: the rim facing south, x 256-287, z 732)
     { 0, 669, 4, { 24, 56, 192, 224 }, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, -280, 8, 0, 8, 0, 32 }, // (the ground north of it, a tile higher, z 728-731)
     { 0, 669, 4, { 24, 56, 224, 256 }, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, -280, 0, 0, 8, 0, 32 }, // (and south of it, z 732-735: under the rim)
